# CHANGELOG

## Version 2.0.0
[BREAKING CHANGES]
- JavaScript rewritten without jQuery or js-cookie, using modern JavaScript (ES2015+).
- Sprockets apps using Uglifier must switch to Terser (see README).
- `cookiesalert/cookie` (bundled js-cookie) has been removed. Delete `//= require
cookiesalert/cookie` from your `application.js`.
- The partial no longer sets `window.rails_env` / `window.gtm_code`; settings are stored in `data-*` attributes on the banner (CSP friendly).

[FIXES]
- `gtm_code` is now passed to the JavaScript (before, Google Tag Manager never loaded).
- Google Tag Manager now also loads on later visits after the user has accepted.
- The `denyBtn` option is now applied.
- The cookies policy link in the locales now has a quoted `href`.

[OTHER CHANGES]
- Works with Sprockets, Propshaft, importmap (`import "cookiesalert"`) and
`javascript_include_tag`.
- `gtm_code` is optional in the partial.
- The `cookies_consent` cookie is set with `SameSite=Lax`.
- Removed the `console.log` on accept.
- Locales are now included in the packaged gem.


## Version 1.0.0
- Breaking change: cookies_alert is now cookies_consent
- cookies_consent is now a Boolean instead of defined/undefined

## Version 0.2.1
- Fix Deny button

## Version 0.2.0
- Adapt gem to GDPR.
- `link` params renamed to `policy_cookies`.
- Add locales in order to easy use.
- Now can deny cookies with deny button.
- New param `gtm_code` for Google Tag Manager code when user accept cookies.
- Bump [js-cookie](https://github.com/js-cookie/js-cookie) to v3.0.1.
